invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the incomplete addition leaves out the step that takes 2r from
  x3_numerator, so X3 and Y3 come out for another point. No fault
  follows: every coordinate is still a field element. bin/p256_equiv_test
  holds the addition to the complete one on multiples of G and table
  entries, and every base multiplication runs it 41 times.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_add(&t, &r, &r);
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&x3_numerator, &x3_numerator, &t);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_add(&t, &r, &r);
